Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: validate EEE AN status reads and C22 transport

The vendor AN-completion check in genphy_c45_read_eee_lpa tests register
bits without checking either read for a negative errno. -EOPNOTSUPP from
a Clause 45-only RollBall bridge has BMSR_ANEGCOMPLETE set when treated as
an integer bitmap, so an unsupported read can wrongly permit reading and
reporting link-partner EEE capabilities before negotiation is complete.

Propagate MDIO read errors. When C45 AN is not complete and the bus has
no C22 read callback, return not-ready without issuing unsupported C22 I/O.
Keep the existing C22 fallback for transports that implement it. Do not
change EEE enable settings or any advertised speed.
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/phy-c45.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/phy-c45.c
@@ -800,10 +800,18 @@
 	/* Auto negotiation complete bit must be set to read correct lpa's EEE.
 	 */
 	val = phy_read_mmd(phydev, MDIO_MMD_AN, MDIO_STAT1);
+	if (val < 0)
+		return val;
 	if (!(val & MDIO_AN_STAT1_COMPLETE)) {
-		/* Some devices rely on CL22 to detect AN complete. */
+		/* Some devices rely on CL22 to detect AN complete. A C45-only
+		 * transport cannot provide that fallback; EEE is not ready.
+		 */
+		if (!phydev->mdio.bus->read)
+			return 0;
 		val = phy_read(phydev, MII_BMSR);
-		if(!(val & BMSR_ANEGCOMPLETE))
+		if (val < 0)
+			return val;
+		if (!(val & BMSR_ANEGCOMPLETE))
 			return 0;
 	}
 
